@startuml CDN_Architecture

title CDN — Latency Improvement + 2 Strategies

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam shadowing false

skinparam rectangle {
    BorderColor #333333
    FontColor #222222
}
skinparam package {
    BorderColor #555555
    FontColor #222222
}

package "Without CDN (Brazil user -> US East server)" as Without #FDFEFE {
    rectangle "TCP Handshake: 600ms\nHTML req/res: 400ms\nAssets req: 200ms\nAssets load: 2000ms\n\nTOTAL: ~3.2 seconds" as W1 #F5B7B1
}

package "With CDN (Brazil user -> nearby edge server)" as With #FDFEFE {
    rectangle "TCP Handshake: 150ms\nHTML req/res: 100ms\nAssets req + load: 550ms\n\nTOTAL: ~800ms" as W2 #A9DFBF
}

Without -[hidden]right-> With

rectangle "CDN\n(Caches content on edge servers,\nphysically closer to users)" as CDN #AED6F1

With -down-> CDN

package "2 Integration Strategies" as Strategies #F4F6F7 {

    rectangle "Pull Strategy\n\nCDN fetches from origin\non first request + TTL expiry" as Pull #F9E79F

    rectangle "Push Strategy\n\nYou manually publish/\nrepublish content to CDN" as Push #D2B4DE
}

CDN -down-> Strategies

note bottom of Pull
  + Low maintenance
  - First request = cache miss (slow)
  - Same TTL for all = expiry spikes
  - Origin still needs decent uptime
end note

note bottom of Push
  + Less traffic to origin server
  + Origin downtime doesn't affect users
  - Must republish on every content change
  - Best for rarely-changing content
end note

rectangle "Benefits: Performance + Availability + Security\n(DDoS mitigation via distributed edge network)" as Benefits #EAECEE

Strategies -down-> Benefits

@enduml
